WEBVTT

00:06.317 --> 00:08.028
...four-term
incumbent Gotham mayor

00:08.028 --> 00:11.740
Don Mitchell, Jr., was
found murdered last night in...

00:11.740 --> 00:13.491
...his tough war on drugs...

00:15.035 --> 00:16.453
...notorious Mafia
crime figure,

00:16.453 --> 00:17.537
Salvatore Maroni...

00:17.537 --> 00:18.913
...sources tell GC1

00:18.913 --> 00:21.332
that a warrant
for Falcone's arrest

00:21.332 --> 00:23.001
is suspected to reach...

00:23.001 --> 00:25.045
...the second
high-profile murder

00:25.045 --> 00:26.171
in as many nights.

00:26.171 --> 00:28.506
This time, the killer
hasn't come forward to claim...

00:29.424 --> 00:30.967
We interrupt
election coverage now

00:30.967 --> 00:32.135
for some breaking news.

00:32.135 --> 00:34.179
We are getting
unconfirmed reports

00:34.179 --> 00:38.266
about a series of explosions
along the city's seawall.

00:39.142 --> 00:42.437
And we are live
watching the Batman vigilante

00:42.437 --> 00:44.189
atop Gotham Square Garden

00:44.189 --> 00:46.941
helping save the lives
of hundreds of injured victims

00:47.067 --> 00:49.778
after devastating explosions
took out the city's seawall.

00:49.778 --> 00:51.196
We will rebuild.

00:52.364 --> 00:53.656
But not just our city.

00:53.656 --> 00:57.202
Together, we will learn
to believe in Gotham again.

00:57.202 --> 00:58.328
It's been a week

00:58.328 --> 01:00.288
since the terrorist
known as The Riddler

01:00.288 --> 01:01.915
blew up Gotham's seawall.

01:01.915 --> 01:03.458
And as the death toll climbs,

01:03.458 --> 01:05.835
Gotham residents are demanding
answers from authorities.

01:05.835 --> 01:08.171
While the wealthier suburbs
have been spared,

01:08.171 --> 01:10.215
it's Gotham's
poorest neighborhoods

01:10.215 --> 01:13.051
that have been hit the hardest,
especially in Crown Point.

01:13.051 --> 01:15.178
Looting and rioting
have become the norm.

01:15.178 --> 01:17.680
Combined with the scarcity
of illicit drugs

01:17.680 --> 01:19.474
and an increase
in gang warfare,

01:19.474 --> 01:21.810
the city has reached
a boiling point.

01:21.935 --> 01:24.688
The murder of longtime mob boss
Carmine Falcone

01:24.688 --> 01:26.314
outside the Iceberg Lounge

01:26.314 --> 01:28.983
has complicated efforts
to restore order,

01:28.983 --> 01:32.153
creating a power vacuum
in Gotham's underworld.

01:32.779 --> 01:33.988
Rumors are swirling

01:33.988 --> 01:36.408
that Carmine's son,
Alberto Falcone,

01:36.408 --> 01:38.243
is set
to take his father's place

01:38.368 --> 01:40.578
despite his public struggles
with alcohol.

01:41.121 --> 01:42.789
After this shakeup
in leadership,

01:42.789 --> 01:44.874
insiders worry
about their future

01:44.874 --> 01:48.461
within the Falcone organization
and wonder what will become

01:48.461 --> 01:51.131
of Gotham's
most notorious family.

04:09.894 --> 04:12.981
Oh, beautiful.
Beautiful, beautiful, beautiful.

04:28.204 --> 04:30.248
I see you've made yourself
at home.

04:32.751 --> 04:35.462
Hey, Alberto, you're here.

04:36.254 --> 04:38.465
Good. Saves me a trip.

04:38.465 --> 04:40.175
What the fuck
are you talking about?

04:40.175 --> 04:42.635
These jewels belong to you.

04:43.261 --> 04:44.512
Your dad made that clear.

04:45.138 --> 04:46.097
But some of the guys,

04:46.097 --> 04:48.600
well, you know,
they're goddamn scavengers.

04:48.600 --> 04:50.518
So I thought I'd do you a solid.

04:50.518 --> 04:52.020
As a show of support for...

04:53.313 --> 04:54.356
your new position.

04:55.690 --> 04:56.524
Well...

04:57.233 --> 04:58.401
congratulations.

04:59.736 --> 05:02.155
I only wish it had been
under different circumstances.

05:02.906 --> 05:03.740
Carmine...

05:05.158 --> 05:06.117
he was a...

05:07.369 --> 05:08.578
He was a great man.

05:09.579 --> 05:11.247
You got some big shoes to fill.

05:14.042 --> 05:16.044
Not too big.

05:16.044 --> 05:18.421
I mean, you know,
manageable shoes.

05:18.421 --> 05:20.215
You think I'm an idiot?

05:20.799 --> 05:22.133
You greedy prick.

05:22.133 --> 05:23.635
My father's been dead a week.

05:23.635 --> 05:25.053
Hey, Al.

05:27.514 --> 05:28.473
You all right?

05:29.474 --> 05:32.143
'Cause we keep a stash
in the loft if you want a hit.

05:33.937 --> 05:35.063
That's not why I'm here.

05:35.063 --> 05:36.606
Of course not.
I was only saying--

05:36.606 --> 05:37.774
You don't get it.

05:37.774 --> 05:39.192
Everyone's looking to me now.

05:39.776 --> 05:42.153
I got this deal going, and...

05:44.406 --> 05:46.408
I can't. I gotta
keep my head on straight.

05:46.408 --> 05:47.826
Yeah, you're right, Boss.

05:47.951 --> 05:49.828
I got no idea
the pressure you're under.

05:51.705 --> 05:54.499
But you're
Alberto Friggin' Falcone,

05:55.542 --> 05:57.544
the new kingpin of Gotham.

06:00.130 --> 06:01.631
We should celebrate that.

06:03.299 --> 06:07.178
Listen, staying off the Drops,
good on you.

06:08.471 --> 06:09.848
But booze don't count.

06:10.432 --> 06:11.266
Does it?

06:18.898 --> 06:20.358
So this new deal
you got going...

06:21.109 --> 06:22.444
Maybe I can help.

06:22.444 --> 06:24.571
You know what
I like most about you, Oz?

06:25.155 --> 06:27.157
You are who you are,

06:27.157 --> 06:28.867
and you couldn't change
if you tried.

06:28.867 --> 06:30.994
Ain't that what makes me fun?

06:36.791 --> 06:38.334
Yeah, go on.

06:39.044 --> 06:39.961
This shit's good.

06:39.961 --> 06:40.962
Good.

06:41.504 --> 06:44.799
But after a while,
you get curious.

06:44.799 --> 06:46.760
There's gotta be something else
out there,

06:47.552 --> 06:49.054
a new kind of high.

06:49.971 --> 06:51.181
So you're gonna, what?

06:52.057 --> 06:53.308
Alter the formula?

06:53.308 --> 06:55.894
We're not just adding ketchup
to fries, man.

06:55.894 --> 06:59.272
I'm talking about
revolutionizing the game.

06:59.981 --> 07:02.275
Fuck. Look at you salivating.

07:03.443 --> 07:04.277
Fine.

07:06.571 --> 07:07.655
You got a girl?

07:08.323 --> 07:09.824
Good-looking guy like you...

07:11.368 --> 07:12.369
Here.

07:13.411 --> 07:14.788
Just keep quiet.

07:14.788 --> 07:17.457
I can't have Viti and those guys
knowing what I've got going

07:17.457 --> 07:19.542
until this new drug's
up on its feet.

07:21.586 --> 07:22.587
Thanks, Boss. It's...

07:24.839 --> 07:26.132
real generous.

07:26.132 --> 07:28.176
Pop always said
you were a good soldier.

07:28.718 --> 07:30.345
It's what he liked most
about you.

07:32.180 --> 07:34.182
But he also knew
you were a dirty soldier

07:34.182 --> 07:35.975
who skims money off the top.

07:37.018 --> 07:39.229
It's okay, man.
You were smart about it.

07:39.229 --> 07:41.106
Never took enough
for Pop to mind.

07:41.773 --> 07:42.899
See, he knew what it meant

07:42.899 --> 07:44.901
for a guy like you
to get a piece.

07:46.236 --> 07:47.445
How it made you feel.

07:48.321 --> 07:50.031
And that was good for business.

07:50.657 --> 07:54.244
Carmine Falcone was a master
at the carrot and stick.

07:57.539 --> 07:58.623
See what I got on?

07:59.791 --> 08:02.043
Your dad's ring. Nice.

08:02.043 --> 08:03.420
Wasn't always his.

08:04.462 --> 08:05.922
Used to be Salvatore's.

08:07.173 --> 08:09.884
- Salvatore Maroni?
- He wore Sal's ring as a trophy.

08:09.884 --> 08:11.553
The ultimate fuck-you.

08:12.512 --> 08:15.098
This is power, right?

08:17.434 --> 08:18.268
Wanna try it on?

08:19.102 --> 08:19.936
Nah.

08:20.395 --> 08:21.229
It's yours.

08:22.647 --> 08:23.481
Yeah.

08:27.444 --> 08:28.570
I don't know, man.

08:30.405 --> 08:31.823
You think I could be
as good as him?

08:32.991 --> 08:34.492
Get his kind of respect?

08:36.411 --> 08:37.245
Your father?

08:39.998 --> 08:40.999
Sure, Boss.

08:42.167 --> 08:43.001
If you want.

08:43.668 --> 08:45.503
But there are different kinds
of power.

08:48.506 --> 08:49.382
When I was kid,

08:50.467 --> 08:51.509
there was a gangster,

08:52.343 --> 08:53.762
real old-school type,

08:54.804 --> 08:55.930
Rex Calabrese.

08:56.931 --> 08:57.891
He was a big deal.

08:58.433 --> 09:00.185
Yeah. At least,
in my neighborhood.

09:01.519 --> 09:02.562
He helped people.

09:03.855 --> 09:05.565
When someone in your family
was sick,

09:06.107 --> 09:07.567
he'd find you a doctor.

09:08.943 --> 09:11.654
Short on rent,
front you the cash.

09:13.323 --> 09:14.783
Knew everyone's names, too.

09:16.826 --> 09:19.120
I don't know how he kept them
all in his head, but...

09:19.746 --> 09:20.997
He saw you on the street,

09:22.082 --> 09:23.124
he'd call out to you,

09:23.875 --> 09:24.751
ask how you were.

09:26.461 --> 09:27.712
Felt like he meant it, too.

09:31.424 --> 09:32.967
When I'm 14 or something,

09:33.843 --> 09:35.303
he has a heart attack and dies,

09:36.596 --> 09:38.014
still holding his cigar.

09:39.516 --> 09:40.600
In my neighborhood,

09:41.601 --> 09:43.228
they throw a parade
in his honor.

09:44.688 --> 09:46.064
A friggin' parade.

09:47.774 --> 09:49.984
I mean, it wasn't fancy,
but it was the gesture...

09:50.860 --> 09:51.778
the show of love...

09:52.862 --> 09:53.905
of what he meant.

09:55.407 --> 09:56.449
Can you imagine?

09:57.409 --> 09:59.160
To be remembered like that?

09:59.160 --> 10:00.370
Revered?

10:02.163 --> 10:03.039
What is this?

10:06.418 --> 10:09.921
You want me to be like
some small-time asshole?

10:12.298 --> 10:14.008
- Nah, that ain't--
- For what?

10:16.511 --> 10:18.972
Would that make it easier
for you to take what's mine?

10:22.600 --> 10:24.269
Or is this you?

10:25.353 --> 10:26.563
What you want?

10:28.481 --> 10:29.357
No.

10:34.696 --> 10:36.197
Holy shit, it is!

10:38.950 --> 10:40.243
This is your dream.

10:41.202 --> 10:42.662
It's so sweet, too.

10:43.455 --> 10:44.664
And so pathetic.

10:45.415 --> 10:48.877
You really think people'd make
a float of your dumb face

10:48.877 --> 10:52.047
and march it down the street,
chanting your goddamn name?

10:54.924 --> 10:59.179
"Oswald Cobb.
Remember him? What a guy!"

11:01.097 --> 11:02.640
What a little bitch!

11:31.586 --> 11:34.381
Aw, fu--

12:35.275 --> 12:36.276
Hurry up, bro.

12:36.276 --> 12:37.402
Relax. I got it.

12:37.902 --> 12:38.778
Hey, help him out.

12:38.778 --> 12:40.447
Hurry up, man.
Just turn the damn thing.

12:40.447 --> 12:41.823
Hey!

12:43.033 --> 12:43.867
Hey!

12:43.992 --> 12:45.744
- Oh, shi--
- You sons of bitches!

12:45.744 --> 12:46.828
Go! Go!

12:46.828 --> 12:48.538
Get the fuck out of here! Go!

12:48.538 --> 12:50.790
- Oh, shit!
- Hey!

12:50.790 --> 12:52.959
- Wait. Wait. Okay, I'm done.
- Go! Go!

12:52.959 --> 12:55.462
- Please! Please! All right.
- Don't you try and run.

12:55.462 --> 12:58.131
I'm sorry. I-I'm sorry. I'm--

12:58.131 --> 13:00.050
Don't move,
you twat-faced little prick.

13:00.050 --> 13:01.384
Trying to steal my shit!

13:02.427 --> 13:04.054
- Hey!
- Shut the fuck up.

13:04.596 --> 13:07.432
You wanna shout again?
You wanna fucking shout again?

13:07.432 --> 13:08.975
You messed with
the wrong fucking guy

13:08.975 --> 13:10.143
on the wrong fucking night.

13:10.143 --> 13:13.605
P-p-p...

13:13.605 --> 13:15.482
Please, please, please.

13:17.650 --> 13:19.152
Don't, okay, please?

13:21.946 --> 13:24.199
P-please!

13:24.199 --> 13:26.409
- Please, don't--
- Jesus! Take a breath.

13:27.285 --> 13:28.119
What have we got here?

13:32.832 --> 13:34.959
"Victor Aguilar."

13:41.716 --> 13:43.259
I'm keeping your ID.

13:44.886 --> 13:46.012
Walk. That way.

13:53.520 --> 13:54.354
Head first.

13:57.691 --> 13:59.693
Fucking foot! God damn it!

14:06.491 --> 14:08.201
Hey! Hey, look at me.

14:08.201 --> 14:09.577
How far do you think you'd get?

14:10.078 --> 14:12.914
This scumbag,
he disrespected me.

14:12.914 --> 14:14.708
- You gonna disrespect me, Vic?
- No. No.

14:14.708 --> 14:17.502
No. 'Cause you and me,
we're in this together now.

14:18.920 --> 14:19.963
Which means...

14:20.672 --> 14:21.756
I own you.

14:24.884 --> 14:26.469
Look what you
fucking made me do.

14:28.513 --> 14:30.014
You're gonna do
everything I say.

14:31.099 --> 14:33.226
Or else I'll murder you and...

14:33.226 --> 14:34.728
anyone you care about.

14:34.728 --> 14:36.771
- You got it?
- Yeah.

14:37.897 --> 14:39.024
Beautiful.

14:39.024 --> 14:41.192
I feel better. You feel better?

14:42.235 --> 14:43.069
Yeah.

14:43.069 --> 14:44.237
Good.

14:44.237 --> 14:45.947
Now, you wanted my car so badly,

14:46.448 --> 14:47.323
you can drive.

14:51.911 --> 14:52.746
Go on.

15:16.853 --> 15:17.896
Make a left up here.

15:18.938 --> 15:20.148
Okay.

15:31.618 --> 15:32.994
This fucking douchebag...

15:35.080 --> 15:36.289
Here we go.

15:41.669 --> 15:43.588
Got you now, you piece of shit.

15:44.923 --> 15:46.383
S-should I--

16:02.232 --> 16:03.483
What do you think of this?

16:04.484 --> 16:06.653
It's a... little air freshener.

16:09.239 --> 16:10.824
Aqua Paradise.

16:12.325 --> 16:13.785
- You smell it?
- Mm-hmm.

16:13.785 --> 16:14.786
It's nice, huh?

16:18.164 --> 16:19.666
- It's nice, yeah.
- Mm-hmm.

16:20.500 --> 16:21.418
Yeah, it's nice.

16:24.462 --> 16:26.589
194 Tower Avenue.

16:28.133 --> 16:29.634
The old tenement on Sixth.

16:31.219 --> 16:32.470
I'm from the Eastside, too.

16:33.054 --> 16:34.139
I mean, not Crown Point.

16:34.973 --> 16:36.266
Further out from the port.

16:39.602 --> 16:41.187
You ever been
to that corner mart?

16:42.522 --> 16:44.065
Next to the...

16:44.649 --> 16:45.734
Coin-O-Matic?

16:49.696 --> 16:50.655
Buddy's?

16:52.699 --> 16:53.867
Yeah, Buddy's.

16:53.992 --> 16:54.909
Oh, man.

16:55.994 --> 16:57.912
They still sell
those Slush Puppies?

16:58.830 --> 17:00.999
I th-think so.

17:01.708 --> 17:02.792
Me and my brothers,

17:03.585 --> 17:05.670
we used to go there
every day in the summer.

17:05.670 --> 17:08.006
You know, we'd mix the flavors
for a suicide.

17:09.132 --> 17:10.341
You ever mix the flavors?

17:10.341 --> 17:11.259
Huh-uh.

17:12.260 --> 17:13.511
Aw. You missed out.

17:16.473 --> 17:18.641
You know, but I'd like to.

17:19.392 --> 17:21.728
You know, like in the...
in the future.

17:23.730 --> 17:24.731
Take a left here.

17:35.617 --> 17:38.078
Hi, Daddy.
Wanna come party with us?

17:38.078 --> 17:40.205
Nice car. Can I get a ride?

17:41.998 --> 17:45.377
Wh-wh-what about the body?
Is that safe on the street?

17:45.377 --> 17:46.878
Why?
Your friends wanna steal it?

17:48.171 --> 17:50.048
Do me a favor, kid.
Shut your goddamn mouth.

17:50.048 --> 17:53.051
- Lookin' good. Ladies.
- Hey, Oz.

17:53.051 --> 17:54.344
- Who is this?
- Good to see you.

17:54.344 --> 17:55.595
Looks brand-new.

17:55.595 --> 17:57.013
Like what you see, sweetie?

18:21.287 --> 18:22.414
- Hey.
- Oz.

18:23.331 --> 18:24.165
Baby.

18:24.791 --> 18:26.751
- Everything okay?
- Yeah, yeah, yeah.

18:26.751 --> 18:28.128
Who's your friend?

18:31.381 --> 18:32.590
You alone?

18:33.299 --> 18:36.678
I... I ain't trying
to get in your business, but...

18:37.971 --> 18:39.347
I need an alibi.

18:40.432 --> 18:41.808
Ideally, for the whole night.

18:42.892 --> 18:44.102
Sounds like we had fun.

18:44.686 --> 18:46.980
I'm serious, Eve. Yeah.

18:47.564 --> 18:48.565
Can you help me out?

18:49.190 --> 18:51.067
Anytime after 10,
but not before.

18:51.067 --> 18:52.861
All right, that'll work.

18:55.655 --> 18:57.032
Thanks, doll.

18:57.032 --> 18:58.533
I'll call ya.

19:05.957 --> 19:07.417
You hungry?
I'm hungry. Let's go.

19:12.505 --> 19:13.465
Stupid night.

19:21.890 --> 19:23.933
I asked for extra pickles,
and they give me two?

19:24.684 --> 19:26.644
So what, a normal amount
of pickles is one?

19:27.187 --> 19:28.646
Makes no goddamn sense.

19:33.860 --> 19:34.986
You want one of mine?

19:35.695 --> 19:37.030
Do I want one of your pickles?

19:37.614 --> 19:39.908
That your dirty little mouth
touched? No, kid, I don't.

19:39.908 --> 19:40.950
Jesus.

19:43.912 --> 19:45.622
Shit! Would you look at that?

19:47.374 --> 19:49.125
Imagine if you
and your buddies came here

19:49.125 --> 19:50.585
instead of trying
to steal from me.

19:52.796 --> 19:54.464
Coulda saved you
a lot of trouble.

19:54.464 --> 19:55.632
What was your plan anyway?

19:55.632 --> 19:58.551
Sell 'em to a scrapyard
for some extra dough?

20:00.762 --> 20:02.389
You got a dollar
in your wallet, kid.

20:02.389 --> 20:04.140
Can you afford
to think that small?

20:05.809 --> 20:07.060
No goddamn ambition.

20:09.145 --> 20:11.147
Snuff out the fire.
We're losing time.

20:28.707 --> 20:29.708
All right, good here.

20:43.847 --> 20:44.806
On three.

20:47.600 --> 20:49.310
You know what? Just do it.

21:12.125 --> 21:13.126
Hold up there, chief.

21:15.170 --> 21:16.504
There's a nice sunrise
behind you.

21:16.504 --> 21:17.672
You should take a look.

21:20.467 --> 21:21.301
Go on.

21:22.761 --> 21:24.012
Please don't do this. No.

21:25.346 --> 21:26.347
Hey, wait.

21:27.015 --> 21:28.308
No, no, no, no.

21:28.308 --> 21:30.351
Hey, hey, hey, hey!
Whoa, whoa, whoa! Hey!

21:30.351 --> 21:31.394
Stop!

21:33.646 --> 21:34.814
Ever had one of these?

21:49.746 --> 21:50.580
There you go.

21:57.962 --> 21:59.547
His name's Alberto Falcone.

22:00.507 --> 22:02.592
He's the new king--
Well, was the new kingpin

22:02.592 --> 22:03.885
of the Falcone mob.

22:06.096 --> 22:06.930
Yeah.

22:07.514 --> 22:09.057
So, the smart play here
is to kill you

22:09.057 --> 22:10.600
and stuff you in the trunk
with Stinky,

22:10.600 --> 22:12.394
- be done with both of youse.
- No, no, no.

22:12.394 --> 22:13.520
We-we don't have to--

22:13.645 --> 22:15.563
It's a goddamn fact, Vic.
It just is.

22:15.563 --> 22:17.899
No, no, no, no, no.
Wait. Wait! Hold on!

22:18.483 --> 22:19.359
You can't.

22:21.027 --> 22:22.153
I could help you.

22:22.696 --> 22:23.571
You know?

22:25.031 --> 22:26.741
With whatever you need,
I can help you.

22:26.741 --> 22:28.201
Yeah. And how do I need you?

22:31.538 --> 22:32.664
I got ambition.

22:33.581 --> 22:36.376
And I'm not...
I'm not a waste, okay? I'm not.

22:36.376 --> 22:39.379
I could... I could help you
w-with whatever it is.

22:39.379 --> 22:42.549
Wh-wh-whatever you need,
whatever it is, all right?

22:43.133 --> 22:44.342
I just--

22:45.301 --> 22:46.845
Please, I need a chance.

22:48.346 --> 22:50.432
- I need a chance!
- All right, calm down.

23:03.862 --> 23:06.156
Well, maybe it'd be useful,
keeping you around.

23:06.156 --> 23:07.073
For now.

23:08.158 --> 23:09.451
See if you got what you say.

23:10.994 --> 23:12.537
But if you step out of line
just once,

23:12.537 --> 23:14.789
I swear to God, I'll gut you
like a fucking fish.

23:14.789 --> 23:15.707
Do you understand?

23:15.707 --> 23:17.500
Yeah. Yeah. Yes.

23:17.500 --> 23:19.002
- Do you understand?
- Yeah. Yeah.

23:19.002 --> 23:20.128
Good.

23:23.923 --> 23:24.966
Now, shut the fuck up.

23:26.051 --> 23:27.343
I wanna watch the sunrise.

24:01.294 --> 24:02.796
We ain't got a lot of time.

24:03.880 --> 24:05.173
I gotta be at work soon.

24:06.424 --> 24:08.843
'Cause, you know,
it's any other day.

24:11.012 --> 24:12.722
You can use the sink
to clean up.

24:14.599 --> 24:16.059
Touch anything, I'll know.

25:27.130 --> 25:28.173
Look at this.

25:29.674 --> 25:31.676
What that fucking madman did.

25:54.407 --> 25:55.909
Hey, Nick, come here.

25:55.909 --> 25:58.453
Bring a pen
and one of them envelopes.

25:59.537 --> 26:00.372
What's up?

26:01.581 --> 26:04.084
Get this to Councilman Hady.

26:04.876 --> 26:07.545
He's a... big fan of Bella Reál.

26:09.005 --> 26:09.839
He...

26:10.548 --> 26:12.759
likes to tout himself
as one of the good ones,

26:13.426 --> 26:15.678
but he got into
some serious debt with Carmine.

26:15.678 --> 26:17.847
We all got our own vices.

26:18.515 --> 26:19.641
All right.

26:20.225 --> 26:22.185
Make sure he knows
it's from me, all right?

26:22.185 --> 26:23.353
Come on, kid.

26:29.609 --> 26:31.403
Hey, Doc. How we lookin'?

26:31.403 --> 26:34.030
Well, we've recovered
about 30% of the product.

26:34.030 --> 26:35.865
There's a risk of contamination.

26:35.865 --> 26:38.034
Most of the Drops
were fished out of sewer water.

26:38.034 --> 26:40.370
That ain't gonna stop Dropheads
from buying it.

26:40.370 --> 26:42.163
- No.
- Give the people what they want.

26:42.163 --> 26:43.415
All right.

26:43.415 --> 26:44.916
Get him in.

26:44.916 --> 26:46.126
What the fuck is that?

26:48.795 --> 26:50.088
Mikey, what the hell happened?

26:50.088 --> 26:51.881
Got jumped by the Odessa Mob, maybe.

26:51.881 --> 26:53.883
Or Burnley Town.
I don't know. It happened fast.

26:53.883 --> 26:55.719
But they got
the whole fucking stash.

26:55.719 --> 26:57.887
- What the fuck? Son of a bitch!
- Yep.

26:57.887 --> 27:00.181
Now we got every asshole
on the street testing fences.

27:00.181 --> 27:01.307
- It's fucking crazy.
- Oz!

27:01.307 --> 27:02.851
- What?
- It's the Family.

27:02.851 --> 27:04.310
- They wanna talk to you.
- Yeah.

27:04.853 --> 27:05.937
Get him outta here, to the back.

27:05.937 --> 27:07.355
You got it.
Let's get the man up.

27:10.108 --> 27:11.568
Let's go, buddy.

27:11.568 --> 27:12.485
Come on.

27:14.988 --> 27:15.822
Yeah.

27:23.747 --> 27:27.000
So, what does that...
what does that mean exactly,

27:27.000 --> 27:28.460
to... to be called in?

27:29.085 --> 27:30.045
Could mean anything.

27:30.045 --> 27:32.964
Do you... do you think
that they know?

27:32.964 --> 27:34.049
Jesus, kid.

27:34.632 --> 27:36.384
Am I holding
a fucking crystal ball?

27:41.681 --> 27:43.058
It's all a song and dance.

27:43.767 --> 27:45.435
Nine times out of ten,
these top-tier guys

27:45.435 --> 27:47.145
wanna meet face-to-face
to feel big,

27:47.270 --> 27:48.938
so I make myself small,

27:48.938 --> 27:50.273
they feel better
about themselves,

27:50.273 --> 27:51.649
and I get to go back to work.

27:53.777 --> 27:54.611
This is us.

28:06.581 --> 28:07.791
Damn!

28:19.386 --> 28:21.179
All right, listen,
if I don't come out...

28:25.475 --> 28:26.726
Nah, I'll be fine.

28:26.726 --> 28:28.770
You'll be fine.
It's gonna be fine.

28:31.147 --> 28:33.316
I'm messing with you, kid.
All right, just sit tight.

28:33.316 --> 28:34.734
Maybe look
for your sense of humor.

28:34.734 --> 28:36.403
It's gotta be here somewhere.

28:51.960 --> 28:52.877
Fellas.

29:01.344 --> 29:02.679
Johnny. Milos.

29:02.679 --> 29:03.930
Have a seat.

29:07.892 --> 29:11.021
Lot of pomp and circumstance
to be coming out here like this.

29:12.188 --> 29:13.440
Not that I'm complaining.

29:17.318 --> 29:19.779
So, we got something
to celebrate or what?

29:20.780 --> 29:22.407
We've decided
to shut down the plant.

29:22.991 --> 29:25.243
We're gonna move all operations
to Robbinsville.

29:25.827 --> 29:26.870
Hold up.

29:27.662 --> 29:28.955
What are you talking about?

29:28.955 --> 29:31.291
There's a lot less heat
in Robbinsville.

29:31.291 --> 29:33.209
Yeah, there's
a lot less business, too.

29:33.877 --> 29:35.920
You know how much cash
my guys bring in?

29:35.920 --> 29:38.339
This is my operation.
You can't just shut it down.

29:38.840 --> 29:39.716
No.

29:40.216 --> 29:42.719
This is our operation.
It's our guys.

29:42.719 --> 29:45.221
You work for the Family.
Have you forgotten that?

29:45.930 --> 29:47.807
Oz, we're consolidating.

29:47.807 --> 29:49.934
Most of the supplies,
they were damaged in the flood.

29:49.934 --> 29:51.102
Actually, that ain't true.

29:51.102 --> 29:53.355
Nah, we recovered
a lot of the product, 70%.

29:53.355 --> 29:55.398
It doesn't matter, all right?
The police are circling.

29:55.398 --> 29:57.150
Got a target on our back.
Gangs encroaching.

29:57.150 --> 29:59.027
There's blood in the water.
Everyone knows it.

29:59.027 --> 30:00.653
- And you wanna bail?
- Jesus Christ!

30:00.653 --> 30:02.530
If we don't protect what's ours,
we look weak.

30:02.530 --> 30:03.531
This isn't your call.

30:03.531 --> 30:05.533
You're handing the Maronis
or someone worse

30:05.533 --> 30:07.494
the keys to the fucking kingdom.
Don't you get that?

30:07.494 --> 30:09.788
The last thing we need
is a goddamn gang war!

30:09.788 --> 30:11.998
Now, Milos asked you here
as a courtesy,

30:11.998 --> 30:13.583
because he's a courteous guy.

30:13.583 --> 30:14.501
I am not.

30:15.085 --> 30:16.294
You will do as you're told.

30:19.005 --> 30:19.839
You're free to leave.

30:24.052 --> 30:25.845
Well, wait a second.

30:29.349 --> 30:30.892
What if I could fix it?

30:30.892 --> 30:31.851
This?

30:32.435 --> 30:35.188
I mean, at the end of the day,
this is all about money, right?

30:35.939 --> 30:38.441
Maybe we don't see eye-to-eye
on every little thing.

30:38.441 --> 30:39.984
You know,
maybe you don't like me.

30:40.610 --> 30:42.862
That's fine.
I'm an acquired taste.

30:43.571 --> 30:44.656
But I make you money.

30:45.532 --> 30:46.991
And I got wind
of a shipment coming in.

30:47.826 --> 30:50.328
I don't wanna tout it too much,
but it's big.

30:50.328 --> 30:51.621
In fact, it's got the potential

30:51.621 --> 30:53.498
to revolutionize
the drug business.

30:54.749 --> 30:57.794
- What kind of shipment?
- I can't reveal the details yet.

30:57.794 --> 30:59.462
Nah, nah, but it's brand-new.

31:00.630 --> 31:02.841
Something that'll help us
expand beyond Drops.

31:03.550 --> 31:06.261
And all you guys gotta do is
sit back and reap the rewards.

31:06.261 --> 31:07.804
I'll oversee the whole thing.

31:07.804 --> 31:10.223
I'll use some of the crew.
I'll run it out of the plant.

31:16.896 --> 31:17.897
Was that a yes or...?

31:18.523 --> 31:20.984
Sofia, please, join us.

31:20.984 --> 31:22.527
Oh, I didn't mean to interrupt.

31:27.365 --> 31:29.367
Oz, you remember
Carmine's daughter?

31:29.367 --> 31:30.368
Yeah.

31:31.036 --> 31:31.953
Sofia...

31:32.454 --> 31:34.330
I thought you were still at...

31:37.083 --> 31:38.960
- Arkham?
- Yeah.

31:40.462 --> 31:41.296
No.

31:42.922 --> 31:44.591
I've been rehabilitated.

31:46.760 --> 31:48.720
Have you asked him
about my brother?

31:50.221 --> 31:52.849
- I thought we agreed--
- Have you heard from Alberto?

31:53.558 --> 31:55.351
- Sofia, please...
- Al?

31:55.351 --> 31:57.562
He went out last night,
he refused his bodyguards,

31:57.562 --> 31:58.897
and he never came home.

31:58.897 --> 31:59.856
Sofia, that's enough.

32:01.858 --> 32:03.860
I better get out of your hair.

32:04.694 --> 32:06.321
You know, let you...

32:07.197 --> 32:09.032
So we can talk about this again?

32:09.616 --> 32:10.658
Shut it down.

32:11.284 --> 32:12.786
You have 48 hours.

32:15.330 --> 32:16.164
I'll get it done.

32:16.748 --> 32:18.917
You know, whatever...
whatever helps the Family.

32:20.627 --> 32:22.796
And it's good to see you.

32:33.431 --> 32:34.724
Fuckin' assholes.

32:37.936 --> 32:38.770
Oz.

32:39.479 --> 32:40.355
A moment.

32:41.439 --> 32:42.982
You never gave me an answer.

32:43.983 --> 32:45.276
Have you seen Alberto?

32:45.276 --> 32:46.194
Oh, yeah. Right.

32:46.194 --> 32:47.362
No. No.

32:47.362 --> 32:50.532
He's the boss now,
so he's a busy man.

32:51.116 --> 32:52.450
But I'm sure he's fine.

32:53.743 --> 32:55.078
They said the same thing.

32:55.078 --> 32:56.413
- Milos and Johnny?
- Mm-hmm.

32:56.413 --> 32:57.330
Well, they'd know.

33:00.750 --> 33:01.584
Well...

33:02.836 --> 33:03.837
Better get back to it.

33:05.088 --> 33:06.297
This is yours?

33:07.674 --> 33:09.592
This? Yeah.

33:11.845 --> 33:12.804
Purple.

33:14.097 --> 33:14.931
Very subtle.

33:14.931 --> 33:17.600
Well, technically, it's plum,
you know?

33:17.600 --> 33:19.519
Leather seats
come standard, too, so...

33:21.604 --> 33:23.898
You've really moved up
in the world, haven't you?

33:29.904 --> 33:30.989
What happened here?

33:33.074 --> 33:36.161
Punk kids tried to steal my rims
a few days back.

33:36.161 --> 33:37.579
I missed,
but they got the message.

33:39.414 --> 33:41.791
We're long overdue
for a catch-up, you and me.

33:43.168 --> 33:44.419
Let's get a bite to eat.

33:47.672 --> 33:48.965
- Right now?
- Right now.

33:50.383 --> 33:51.468
I know a place.

34:10.278 --> 34:12.197
Another dirty martini.
Three olives.

34:12.197 --> 34:13.531
You ready for another one?

34:13.656 --> 34:16.159
- You can make that two actually.
- Right away.

34:19.579 --> 34:22.374
It's a bit stuffy for my tastes.

34:22.374 --> 34:24.084
My father used to bring
me and Alberto here

34:24.084 --> 34:25.210
when we were kids.

34:28.088 --> 34:30.507
He paid us to keep our elbows
off the table.

34:32.384 --> 34:33.968
Well, who's stopping you now, huh?

34:37.680 --> 34:38.598
There you go.

34:47.107 --> 34:49.109
You think they're wondering
if it's really me?

34:51.111 --> 34:51.986
Well, I would.

34:52.737 --> 34:56.241
What, is a psycho killer
just roaming around free,

34:56.241 --> 34:57.200
having a salad?

34:59.077 --> 35:00.328
What did the Gazette call me?

35:01.079 --> 35:02.205
The Hangman?

35:03.707 --> 35:05.792
The guards insisted
that I read every article,

35:05.792 --> 35:07.168
that I see all the stories.

35:08.086 --> 35:09.713
If only I'd been
a dutiful daughter.

35:15.427 --> 35:16.761
Are you nervous, Oz?

35:17.637 --> 35:18.513
Nervous?

35:20.432 --> 35:22.350
I'd hate for you
to feel nervous with me.

35:23.977 --> 35:26.312
'Cause despite what you
might think, I don't blame you.

35:26.312 --> 35:28.898
You know, if you hadn't gone
to my father...

35:30.525 --> 35:32.193
He left you no choice.

35:32.193 --> 35:35.280
Yeah, sure.
But I coulda done something--

35:35.280 --> 35:36.197
Let's not do that.

35:36.781 --> 35:37.866
Daddy is dead.

35:38.908 --> 35:40.035
And we are...

35:42.078 --> 35:43.246
untamed.

35:53.006 --> 35:55.300
Alberto told me he was going
to your club last night

35:55.300 --> 35:56.843
to get to my father's loft.

36:00.388 --> 36:03.349
I insisted I go with him, but...
he's been so protective of me.

36:03.349 --> 36:04.934
He didn't want me
leaving the house.

36:06.144 --> 36:09.230
It was all part of this plan
he cooked up.

36:09.230 --> 36:10.899
It was our shared secret.

36:11.566 --> 36:14.819
But then today, I hear you

36:14.819 --> 36:17.614
talking about revolutionizing
the drug business,

36:17.614 --> 36:19.157
and it just doesn't sit right.

36:20.950 --> 36:22.744
How do you know about his plan,

36:22.744 --> 36:25.997
and why on Earth
would you pitch it as your own?

36:28.833 --> 36:31.836
You know, it's so brazen

36:32.879 --> 36:36.383
that you either have to be
blindingly stupid

36:36.925 --> 36:38.176
or wildly confident

36:38.176 --> 36:40.929
that he isn't coming back
to reclaim it.

36:40.929 --> 36:43.056
So, I'm going to ask you again.

36:44.891 --> 36:46.434
Do you know where my brother is?

36:47.977 --> 36:49.145
Listen, Sofia...

36:53.441 --> 36:54.484
I'm an asshole.

36:56.319 --> 36:57.862
But you're the surprise here.

36:58.822 --> 36:59.948
Excuse me?

36:59.948 --> 37:01.783
Al never told me you was back...

37:02.784 --> 37:04.828
or that you were in on
this thing with us.

37:04.828 --> 37:07.288
Yeah, he's keeping us both
in the dark,

37:07.288 --> 37:08.415
and I don't know why.

37:09.582 --> 37:12.085
But you're right.
Alberto trusted me.

37:12.085 --> 37:14.879
And my stupid mouth...
You know, I screwed up.

37:16.214 --> 37:17.757
Maybe you could put in
a good word.

37:18.425 --> 37:20.593
I mean, I don't wanna
put that on you, but...

37:22.053 --> 37:23.847
He was so passionate
about his plan,

37:23.847 --> 37:25.974
I thought there's no reason
not to move forward,

37:25.974 --> 37:28.101
just 'cause he's
on another bender, you know?

37:28.101 --> 37:30.979
I mean, the shipment arrives
in a few days, right?

37:32.605 --> 37:33.898
What do you mean "a bender"?

37:37.902 --> 37:39.529
Al's an addict, sweetheart.

37:40.655 --> 37:42.115
He's got a penchant for Drops.

37:42.949 --> 37:44.534
And booze and gambling.

37:44.534 --> 37:46.244
I'm pretty sure
he's got a sex thing, too.

37:46.244 --> 37:48.663
So yeah, this ain't
the first time he's gone AWOL.

37:48.663 --> 37:50.123
But he always comes back.

37:51.041 --> 37:54.794
Look, if he was at my club,
I wouldn't know.

37:56.087 --> 37:57.422
I was actually
drowning my sorrows

37:57.422 --> 37:59.507
with my lady friend
last night, Eve.

38:02.302 --> 38:04.596
If it'll make you feel better,
let's you and me go there now.

38:04.596 --> 38:05.889
Come on. We'll scour the joint.

38:05.889 --> 38:08.516
I doubt anything will turn up,
but it's worth a shot.

38:09.100 --> 38:10.935
You know, whatever puts
your mind at ease.

38:15.899 --> 38:16.900
No, Oz, you're right.

38:19.277 --> 38:20.779
I'm probably just being crazy.

38:27.827 --> 38:29.329
Let's stay and enjoy the meal.

38:31.956 --> 38:33.958
I know I could use a good one.

38:33.958 --> 38:35.293
He'll turn up, Sofia.

38:36.628 --> 38:37.504
I'm sure of it.

38:40.048 --> 38:42.217
Thanks for lunch.
I'll get the next one.

38:46.721 --> 38:48.014
You know, Oz,

38:48.014 --> 38:49.849
people underestimate you,
but not me.

38:50.975 --> 38:53.061
I've always known
you were capable of more.

39:13.039 --> 39:14.124
Where are we going?

39:22.048 --> 39:25.468
Are-are we in trouble?

39:40.025 --> 39:42.318
Scan the code.
See Gotham's true face.

39:43.153 --> 39:45.113
- Scan the code?
- Get the fuck outta here.

39:47.157 --> 39:48.450
Irving Grove.

39:48.575 --> 39:50.035
Irving Grove Station.

39:51.745 --> 39:53.288
Irving Grove Station.

39:57.834 --> 39:58.877
This is yours?

40:00.170 --> 40:01.004
Get in.

40:42.170 --> 40:44.089
I ain't never taken
anyone here before.

40:44.756 --> 40:46.007
You say a word to anybody...

40:46.007 --> 40:47.133
You'll gut me like a fish.

40:47.133 --> 40:48.718
Yeah, till you bleed out
and die.

40:51.846 --> 40:54.099
Oh, and mind
your friggin' manners, too.

41:01.022 --> 41:01.856
Here.

41:03.441 --> 41:04.275
Don't move.

41:06.569 --> 41:07.821
What're you doing here?

41:07.821 --> 41:09.364
What do you mean
what am I doing here?

41:09.364 --> 41:10.448
I came to see you.

41:10.573 --> 41:11.908
Huh? Princess.

41:13.910 --> 41:16.621
- You look handsome.
- Thank you.

41:16.621 --> 41:18.957
- Put it on straight.
- Close your eyes.

41:18.957 --> 41:21.209
- I got you something. Come here.
- What did you do?

41:21.209 --> 41:22.460
I'll tell you when.

41:23.503 --> 41:26.047
Wha... Wait. What did you do?

41:26.047 --> 41:28.508
Okay, now look, keep 'em closed.

41:28.508 --> 41:30.009
- They're closed.
- All right.

41:31.886 --> 41:33.138
Open your eyes.

41:36.391 --> 41:38.768
Oswald, it's too much.

41:38.768 --> 41:41.271
- No.
- It's perfect.

41:41.271 --> 41:42.272
It suits ya, Ma.

41:44.607 --> 41:46.234
- Thank you, sweetheart.
- You're welcome.

41:46.359 --> 41:48.069
That's crazy.

41:48.069 --> 41:50.405
Wait, wait, wait.
Was I expecting you?

41:50.405 --> 41:52.032
- It's not Sunday, is it?
- No, it's--

41:52.032 --> 41:54.284
- I didn't get--
- Nah, nah.

41:54.284 --> 41:55.827
No, it's a special occasion.

41:55.827 --> 41:58.038
We're gonna... We're gonna
leave town for a while.

41:58.038 --> 42:00.540
Yeah. Take a little vacation.

42:00.540 --> 42:03.043
A vacation? To where?
You know I hate flying.

42:03.043 --> 42:04.335
Yeah. We're gonna drive.

42:05.003 --> 42:06.004
We're gonna drive?

42:06.004 --> 42:08.423
Who's gonna drive?
You gonna drive?

42:09.090 --> 42:10.550
- Ma?
- What?

42:10.550 --> 42:12.677
Why is this in the tub?
Your pills are ruined.

42:12.677 --> 42:14.345
No. I take 'em every morning
with breakfast.

42:14.345 --> 42:15.847
The tub is full.

42:15.847 --> 42:17.265
The boys were playing
in the bath.

42:17.265 --> 42:18.391
They didn't wanna get out.

42:22.937 --> 42:23.772
What?

42:23.772 --> 42:24.814
Oh, nothing.

42:25.565 --> 42:27.734
How about let's take your meds
right now, huh?

42:29.527 --> 42:30.612
Just to be sure.

42:33.156 --> 42:34.324
I took 'em.

42:34.449 --> 42:35.867
The pills are by the sink.

42:35.867 --> 42:37.243
Oswald!

42:37.827 --> 42:38.953
Someone's here.

42:38.953 --> 42:40.455
- Get out of my house!
- Hi. I'm...

42:40.455 --> 42:43.249
Who the hell is this?
Who the hell are you? What?

42:43.249 --> 42:45.377
- Shit! Ma, sorry. This is Vic.
- Get out!

42:45.377 --> 42:46.920
He's gonna help
take care of you.

42:47.420 --> 42:48.922
Just in case I need
to handle some things

42:48.922 --> 42:50.131
while we're gone. All right?

42:50.131 --> 42:52.425
- Huh. Vic?
- Yeah.

42:52.967 --> 42:55.261
- What is he, a nurse?
- Kinda.

42:55.261 --> 42:57.722
- No, I'm not--
- He's got nurse-like qualities.

42:57.722 --> 43:00.600
I'll explain more
in the car. All right?

43:07.273 --> 43:08.441
All right.

43:09.901 --> 43:10.944
Ma, here's your water.

43:11.069 --> 43:13.822
Take these two pills,
then we gotta go, okay?

43:14.989 --> 43:16.533
There you go, okay?

43:17.283 --> 43:20.036
Will you tell me first
what I did to lose your respect?

43:21.996 --> 43:23.790
- What are you talking about?
- You come in here,

43:23.790 --> 43:25.709
you're trying to buy me off
with a necklace?

43:26.209 --> 43:28.878
Some bullshit about
an urgent special occasion...

43:28.878 --> 43:29.796
Ma.

43:29.796 --> 43:31.756
Did I raise my sons
to lie to me?

43:31.756 --> 43:33.466
- Did I?
- No.

43:33.466 --> 43:35.927
So, then what did you do?
What did you do?

43:35.927 --> 43:37.554
Come on. What did you do?

43:40.014 --> 43:41.015
I...

43:42.517 --> 43:43.643
What did you do?

43:45.562 --> 43:46.521
I shot...

43:48.064 --> 43:49.649
Alberto Falcone.

43:51.109 --> 43:51.985
He's dead.

43:52.902 --> 43:55.280
It ain't safe for you here.
You understand?

43:55.905 --> 43:58.450
Sofia Falcone's out of Arkham,
and she knows.

43:59.826 --> 44:01.369
Or if she don't, she will.

44:01.369 --> 44:02.662
Why'd you shoot him? Why?

44:02.662 --> 44:05.165
Jesus, Ma, I ain't doing this
with you right now, okay?

44:09.377 --> 44:10.462
Fine.

44:12.672 --> 44:14.883
He fuckin' laughed at me.

44:15.967 --> 44:16.801
All right?

44:18.636 --> 44:20.680
- Now, can we go please?
- He laughed at you?

44:20.680 --> 44:23.183
It was impulsive. It was stupid.
Is that what you wanna hear?

44:23.183 --> 44:25.018
Jesus, I'm trying
to take care of you.

44:25.018 --> 44:26.311
- Stop.
- I can't risk it.

44:26.311 --> 44:27.729
I can't risk you.
I'm all you got.

44:27.729 --> 44:29.981
- If something happened to me--
- Stop! Stop talking!

44:31.691 --> 44:33.526
Do you hear the words
coming out of your mouth?

44:33.526 --> 44:35.070
- Yeah.
- How weak they sound?

44:36.696 --> 44:37.989
Like a little pussy boy?

44:39.949 --> 44:40.825
Look at me.

44:41.534 --> 44:42.952
Is that what you are, Oswald?

44:43.953 --> 44:45.580
Weak little pussy boy?

44:45.580 --> 44:46.498
No.

44:48.666 --> 44:49.501
That's right.

44:50.960 --> 44:52.253
'Cause you're mine.

44:52.754 --> 44:54.839
You're my big, strong bull
of a boy.

44:54.839 --> 44:56.341
You never forget that.

44:59.094 --> 45:00.178
Come here.

45:07.769 --> 45:09.145
Don't you see, dear?

45:09.896 --> 45:11.690
What you did wasn't impulsive.

45:12.357 --> 45:13.566
It was instinctual.

45:14.693 --> 45:17.112
You shot that junkie piss-ant

45:17.112 --> 45:18.863
because you wanted to.

45:20.615 --> 45:21.616
Just like that.

45:23.868 --> 45:25.870
Oh, you're so close now
to having

45:25.870 --> 45:27.956
everything you ever wanted,
everything you deserve.

45:27.956 --> 45:30.208
You wanna run? You wanna hide?

45:30.208 --> 45:32.085
No.

45:32.669 --> 45:34.796
This city is meant
to be yours, sweetheart.

45:38.341 --> 45:39.843
What are you gonna do to get it?

45:50.937 --> 45:54.524
Put the blame on Mame, boys

45:55.150 --> 45:57.777
Put the blame on Mame

46:00.822 --> 46:05.410
They once had a shootin'
up in the Klondike

46:05.410 --> 46:08.371
When they got Dan McGrew

46:09.414 --> 46:13.793
Folks were putting the blame on

46:13.793 --> 46:17.464
The lady known as Lou

46:18.715 --> 46:21.092
That's the story
that went around

46:21.092 --> 46:22.510
God damn it, this chick.

46:22.510 --> 46:25.305
But here's the real lowdown

46:27.057 --> 46:30.268
Put the blame on Mame, boys...

46:31.478 --> 46:32.520
Who's Mame?

46:34.272 --> 46:35.273
It don't matter, kid.

46:36.483 --> 46:37.567
That's the thing.

46:38.943 --> 46:40.403
She's just a scapegoat.

46:40.403 --> 46:43.698
That's the thing
that slew McGrew

46:44.532 --> 46:48.244
So you can put the blame
on Mame, boys

46:48.244 --> 46:51.915
Put the blame

46:51.915 --> 46:57.504
On Mame

47:00.882 --> 47:03.176
Listen, it ain't easy,
but your part in this...

47:03.760 --> 47:04.928
it's the most important.

47:05.553 --> 47:07.180
So don't say you're good
unless you are.

47:09.516 --> 47:11.518
I don't know, Oz.
I don't know if I'm...

47:13.645 --> 47:16.815
I've-I've n-never done
anything like this.

47:21.945 --> 47:23.154
Listen, Vic...

47:24.280 --> 47:25.657
the tenement where you live...

47:27.033 --> 47:28.201
I know it's gone.

47:28.910 --> 47:30.662
Nothing on Sixth
was left standing.

47:30.662 --> 47:34.249
I don't know if you had family
or people in there...

47:36.251 --> 47:37.252
but you made it.

47:37.836 --> 47:39.212
You're standing right here.

47:40.338 --> 47:41.423
I've been where you are.

47:41.923 --> 47:43.258
And you heard my ma.

47:43.258 --> 47:44.718
I mean, this...

47:44.718 --> 47:47.470
this is one of those moments
where you gotta ask yourself...

47:48.054 --> 47:49.264
what kind of life do I want?

47:50.140 --> 47:52.517
You wanna spend your days
thinking small, stealing rims,

47:52.517 --> 47:53.768
barely getting by?

47:54.769 --> 47:56.187
Or do you want more
for yourself?

47:57.772 --> 47:59.399
You saw how the Falcones live.

48:00.150 --> 48:02.610
Can you imagine
living like that? Huh?

48:02.610 --> 48:06.239
In a mansion,
maids and butlers and shit?

48:06.239 --> 48:07.615
They don't even know
what they got,

48:07.615 --> 48:08.908
'cause they always had it.

48:10.201 --> 48:11.202
Never hungry.

48:11.953 --> 48:12.912
Born full.

48:14.622 --> 48:15.457
Not us.

48:18.209 --> 48:20.545
The world wasn't built
for guys like us.

48:21.713 --> 48:24.215
That's why we gotta take
whatever we decide is ours.

48:25.258 --> 48:27.969
'Cause no one's gonna give it
to us, not without a fight.

48:30.430 --> 48:31.639
Now, I coulda killed you.

48:32.223 --> 48:33.975
I coulda put you
out of your misery,

48:33.975 --> 48:34.976
but I didn't,

48:34.976 --> 48:36.770
'cause you need
a guy like me, Vic.

48:37.896 --> 48:38.897
But I gotta know.

48:40.815 --> 48:41.733
No bullshit.

48:43.985 --> 48:45.528
Can I count on you
to pull through?

48:48.740 --> 48:49.574
Yeah, I...

48:50.200 --> 48:51.159
I can do it.

48:53.495 --> 48:54.662
I can do it.

48:57.957 --> 48:59.084
I know you can.

49:00.668 --> 49:03.129
What do you think? I hire
any schmuck off the street? No.

49:06.925 --> 49:09.052
All right, go ahead.
Get outta here.

49:09.677 --> 49:10.512
Keep your phone on.

49:48.174 --> 49:49.008
Sal.

49:50.176 --> 49:51.469
That's not my table.

50:05.650 --> 50:07.652
Listen, Sal, I'm here
to make things right.

50:08.820 --> 50:10.488
I'm done with the Falcones.

50:10.488 --> 50:13.158
I wanna offer my services
to you and your family.

50:13.158 --> 50:15.827
Well, that surprises me, Oz.
Really does.

50:16.578 --> 50:19.372
'Cause I thought you liked
eating outta Falcone's ass.

50:20.165 --> 50:21.958
Oh, you wanna throw stones?

50:22.959 --> 50:23.793
Fine.

50:24.794 --> 50:25.920
But from where I sit,

50:26.504 --> 50:27.714
and where you sit,

50:28.506 --> 50:29.799
I don't think
you're in a position

50:29.799 --> 50:31.009
not to hear me out.

50:31.634 --> 50:32.719
Way I see it,

50:32.719 --> 50:35.346
the Falcone higher-ups are
a bunch of old men who don't...

50:35.346 --> 50:36.473
No disrespect.

50:36.473 --> 50:37.807
...who don't remember
what it's like

50:37.807 --> 50:39.059
to get their hands dirty.

50:39.059 --> 50:41.269
That's what they hire
guys like me for,

50:41.269 --> 50:43.521
which means I got direct access
to the ground game.

50:44.064 --> 50:46.900
I'm talking the Drops,
the dealers, the chemists,

50:46.900 --> 50:48.026
the whole thing.

50:48.985 --> 50:49.944
Next couple of days,

50:50.070 --> 50:52.822
the Falcones are gonna do
something real stupid,

50:52.822 --> 50:54.741
shut down the biggest
Drops operation they got...

50:54.741 --> 50:56.284
I'm talking millions
of dollars' worth.

50:56.284 --> 50:58.411
...and move to some bumfuck part
of Gotham,

50:59.037 --> 51:00.622
which means a huge chunk
of their business

51:00.622 --> 51:01.915
will be ripe for the taking.

51:03.291 --> 51:04.959
And guess
who's in charge of the move.

51:05.835 --> 51:07.462
I could give you
everything you need.

51:07.462 --> 51:10.840
So your crew could just swoop in
and steal the whole fucking kit.

51:10.840 --> 51:11.966
I play victim.

51:12.801 --> 51:14.219
We split the payday.

51:14.803 --> 51:16.304
You make it sound so simple.

51:17.472 --> 51:19.808
But it's my guys
doing all the heavy lifting.

51:19.808 --> 51:21.851
Yeah, revenge don't come easy.

51:23.061 --> 51:24.312
Come on, Sal.

51:25.563 --> 51:27.357
Don't you fucking miss it?

51:29.609 --> 51:30.443
Respect?

51:32.070 --> 51:34.364
That's really what Carmine stole
from you, ain't it?

51:36.116 --> 51:37.492
He was a dirty rat.

51:38.535 --> 51:40.078
He played us both for fools.

51:40.912 --> 51:42.247
Ain't no changing that.

51:44.374 --> 51:45.375
But he's dead,

51:46.251 --> 51:47.502
and I'm here now,

51:47.502 --> 51:49.546
and I'm offering you
the opportunity of a lifetime.

51:49.546 --> 51:52.048
And this first hit,
it's just the beginning.

51:52.674 --> 51:54.509
I know a lot more
than people think.

51:55.468 --> 51:57.095
I'll keep playing double agent.

51:58.221 --> 51:59.055
You and me,

52:00.515 --> 52:02.100
we can tear down
their fucking empire

52:02.100 --> 52:03.143
from the inside out.

52:07.480 --> 52:09.858
What is it
you're really after, Oz?

52:09.858 --> 52:12.027
I just told you what I'm after.
What do you mean?

52:12.027 --> 52:14.738
I know who you are.
I know what you are.

52:15.363 --> 52:18.241
I don't work with people
whose loyalty is for sale.

52:18.825 --> 52:21.703
You think I forgot all the times
you schmoozed me and my boys

52:21.703 --> 52:23.288
just to turn around and fuck us?

52:23.288 --> 52:24.539
Thought I forgot that?

52:25.999 --> 52:28.585
Huge drug bust does down
right under your nose,

52:28.585 --> 52:30.211
and you got nothing
to do with it?

52:31.421 --> 52:32.505
The fuck outta here.

52:35.800 --> 52:37.927
Look, I can see you're upset.

52:38.553 --> 52:39.804
Trust takes time.

52:40.805 --> 52:42.057
But this ain't bullshit.

52:43.183 --> 52:45.685
Whoever controls Drops
controls the streets.

52:45.685 --> 52:46.895
You know that's right.

52:49.105 --> 52:50.023
So how about this?

52:50.815 --> 52:52.108
I'll come back
in a couple of days...

52:52.108 --> 52:54.527
I never wanna see
your smug face again.

52:54.527 --> 52:56.404
...we'll see
if we can't work something out.

52:57.697 --> 52:59.074
It's good seeing you.
You look good.

52:59.949 --> 53:01.368
- Fuck off.
- Think on it, Sal.

53:05.205 --> 53:06.206
I almost forgot.

53:11.628 --> 53:12.796
Ain't this yours?

53:17.467 --> 53:18.802
Where did you get this?

53:18.802 --> 53:20.595
Carmine. Wore it as his own.

53:22.889 --> 53:23.932
The Falcones...

53:25.517 --> 53:27.519
they been flaunting
what they done to you for years.

53:27.519 --> 53:29.479
But how is it that you have it?

53:31.981 --> 53:33.566
Maybe I'm more
than what you think.

53:43.868 --> 53:46.121
What up? It's Victor.
Leave a message.

53:46.121 --> 53:47.080
Fuck!

54:02.929 --> 54:04.013
Nobody home.

54:08.518 --> 54:09.436
Shit!

54:13.606 --> 54:14.691
Go.

54:16.860 --> 54:18.528
Let's go. Let's go. Let's go.

54:32.834 --> 54:35.170
Come on, Vic. Shit, shit, shit.

54:35.170 --> 54:36.629
What up? It's Victor.

54:36.629 --> 54:37.714
- Shit!
- Leave a message.

54:38.298 --> 54:39.591
Damn it, Vic!

54:56.024 --> 54:56.858
Fuck!

55:06.242 --> 55:07.118
Let's go.

55:13.083 --> 55:14.751
Go. Go, go. Let's go.

55:36.731 --> 55:37.982
Get the fuck out!

55:42.779 --> 55:44.698
Come here!

55:44.698 --> 55:45.949
I'll fucking...

56:13.351 --> 56:14.185
Fuck.

56:16.396 --> 56:19.899
It's a terrible feeling.
Isn't it?

56:21.651 --> 56:23.570
Nothing left to hide behind.

56:24.446 --> 56:27.323
The guards at Arkham
stripped us bare every morning.

56:29.868 --> 56:31.369
It was humiliating...

56:32.579 --> 56:34.039
being turned into a thing.

56:36.583 --> 56:38.877
But after a while, I just
started to think, "Well...

56:39.586 --> 56:42.714
...what's it matter?
There's nothing left anyway."

56:44.507 --> 56:45.675
But my brother?

56:45.675 --> 56:47.886
My brother
visited me every week.

56:49.137 --> 56:52.474
And every week, he said
that there was something left,

56:53.266 --> 56:57.437
and that he was gonna
help me fight to keep it.

56:58.772 --> 57:01.816
I just wonder
how you see me, Oz.

57:03.193 --> 57:08.156
If I am more
than a thing to play with.

57:11.910 --> 57:16.164
You were right, though,
about the club and the loft.

57:16.873 --> 57:17.749
That was all clean.

57:18.917 --> 57:19.918
But outside...

57:21.169 --> 57:22.128
Well...

57:23.004 --> 57:26.633
The downside
of driving a plum car

57:27.467 --> 57:29.427
is that it's very hard
to forget.

57:30.845 --> 57:32.055
And so are you

57:32.055 --> 57:35.266
when you shoot at a bunch
of kids in the street.

57:35.266 --> 57:36.476
And this one...

57:37.143 --> 57:38.728
says it all happened...

57:40.647 --> 57:43.233
the night Alberto went missing.

57:46.194 --> 57:47.070
I don't know.

57:48.905 --> 57:49.823
What do you say?

57:52.575 --> 57:53.910
You think I know this kid?

57:54.744 --> 57:55.829
I don't know this kid.

57:57.205 --> 57:59.165
You can't take
some teenager's word over mine.

57:59.165 --> 58:00.917
So you're saying
that he's the liar?

58:01.835 --> 58:03.670
- Yes!
- Not you?

58:03.670 --> 58:05.505
Yes! Fucking yes!

58:05.505 --> 58:06.798
Okay.

58:06.798 --> 58:08.049
Hey, no. I--

58:14.347 --> 58:17.100
That's what you wanted, right?

58:17.684 --> 58:20.353
To have my reputation
precede me?

58:20.895 --> 58:22.272
You are so good

58:22.272 --> 58:24.274
at talking your way
out of things.

58:24.274 --> 58:28.069
Even at the cost
of someone else's life.

58:28.903 --> 58:30.113
Especially then.

58:30.697 --> 58:31.614
Right?

58:33.116 --> 58:35.243
The fuck you doing?
What are you doing?!

58:35.243 --> 58:37.162
But my father
isn't around anymore

58:37.912 --> 58:39.122
to reward you

58:39.873 --> 58:43.084
with fancy suits,
and stupid cars...

58:43.084 --> 58:44.085
Sofia.

58:44.085 --> 58:47.172
...and a club that he lets
you believe is yours.

58:48.089 --> 58:49.466
Sofia--

58:53.053 --> 58:55.055
It's just you and me now, okay?

58:55.930 --> 58:59.225
So I want you to think.
I want you to really think.

59:01.853 --> 59:02.812
Am I crazy?

59:05.440 --> 59:06.483
Is it all in my head?

59:09.986 --> 59:11.404
Tell me. Tell me.

59:12.238 --> 59:14.574
Tell me that I'm...
that I'm too emotional,

59:14.574 --> 59:17.660
and that I have
an overactive imagination,

59:17.660 --> 59:24.584
and that I shouldn't take things
so personally.

59:29.255 --> 59:30.256
But first...

59:33.426 --> 59:34.677
tell me he's alive.

01:00:02.122 --> 01:00:03.456
Miss Falcone, please.

01:00:06.710 --> 01:00:08.086
What the fuck is this?

01:00:54.883 --> 01:00:55.759
Oh, shit!

01:01:37.509 --> 01:01:38.676
You did good today, kid.

01:01:42.180 --> 01:01:43.098
Thanks.

01:01:43.681 --> 01:01:44.808
So, I gotta ask.

01:01:46.101 --> 01:01:46.935
What happened?

01:01:48.353 --> 01:01:50.188
I mean, we made a plan.
You were there.

01:01:51.231 --> 01:01:52.357
Didn't we agree

01:01:52.357 --> 01:01:54.275
the head alone
would be the most poetic,

01:01:54.275 --> 01:01:55.944
and the pinky,
the cherry on top?

01:01:56.569 --> 01:01:58.279
But instead,
the whole body's in there.

01:01:58.405 --> 01:01:59.447
Just a pinky chopped off.

01:01:59.447 --> 01:02:00.949
It felt...

01:02:02.117 --> 01:02:03.535
well, small.

01:02:03.535 --> 01:02:07.789
Yeah, right. No, I--
Look, I-I-I wanted to, right?

01:02:07.789 --> 01:02:09.499
And I th-thought that I could,
but...

01:02:10.500 --> 01:02:12.043
When I got to it,
and I'm thinking,

01:02:12.711 --> 01:02:16.047
"Do I... Do I start at the front
and then hit the trachea?"

01:02:16.047 --> 01:02:17.424
But then
when I got to his throat,

01:02:17.424 --> 01:02:19.175
I started thinking,
"Do I cut from the back?"

01:02:19.175 --> 01:02:21.010
And then I'm imagining
the spine and...

01:02:21.010 --> 01:02:22.429
All right, all right, all right.

01:02:22.429 --> 01:02:23.680
You know what? It's fine.

01:02:24.305 --> 01:02:25.348
Room to grow.

01:02:25.890 --> 01:02:27.517
Yeah. At least Sofia
got the message.

01:02:28.059 --> 01:02:29.978
With Sal wearing that ring
around Blackgate,

01:02:29.978 --> 01:02:32.063
Maronis ain't got no choice
but to take credit.

01:02:32.522 --> 01:02:33.690
That's what matters.

01:02:34.357 --> 01:02:36.234
Wait. S-Sal doesn't know?

01:02:37.235 --> 01:02:38.987
I thought that
the whole th-thing we--

01:02:38.987 --> 01:02:40.363
Jesus, Vic, relax.

01:02:41.489 --> 01:02:43.033
We just put the Maronis
back on the map.

01:02:43.033 --> 01:02:46.161
If Sal's got a problem
with that, then... fuck him.

01:02:46.161 --> 01:02:47.370
I don't need him.

01:02:47.871 --> 01:02:48.997
I don't need any of 'em.

01:02:50.457 --> 01:02:53.376
From here on out,
there's no more playing it safe.

01:02:54.794 --> 01:02:56.296
Drops are yesterday's game.

01:02:57.714 --> 01:02:59.799
I'm gonna get whatever the hell
is in that shipment.

01:03:00.967 --> 01:03:02.635
I'm gonna run this goddamn city.

01:03:04.804 --> 01:03:05.930
And I want you in on it.

01:03:08.183 --> 01:03:09.017
Really?

01:03:09.017 --> 01:03:10.977
Yeah. You earned it.

01:03:11.853 --> 01:03:13.897
You know, for the most part.

01:03:14.522 --> 01:03:16.775
And guys like us,
we gotta stick together.

01:03:22.280 --> 01:03:24.115
It's better, right? Come on.

01:03:24.115 --> 01:03:25.367
When you mix the flavors?

01:03:26.910 --> 01:03:28.078
Yeah, it's good.

01:03:28.078 --> 01:03:29.913
No. It's not just good.
It's better.

01:03:29.913 --> 01:03:31.122
It's the fucking best.
